  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Backend Setup**\n\nI\'m currently verifying the backend setup, specifically confirming that we\'ll be using a full-stack Express server with Vite middleware, as per the framework guidelines. I\'m also checking the `package.json` scripts to ensure they align with these requirements. I am on schedule, and this should not impact our timeline.\n\n\n**Defining App Features**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the app\'s core features based on user requirements. The focus is on incorporating JLPT N5-N1 modules with Kanji, vocabulary, and grammar for each level. I\'m detailing each section, including example words, definitions, and ensuring Portuguese translations are included for all elements, to ensure a smooth user experience.\n\n\n**Outlining App Modules**\n\nI\'m now outlining the key learning modules. I\'ve designed sections for foundational alphabets like Hiragana and Katakana, complete with interactive study modes that use the Web Speech API for pronunciation, romaji, and mnemonics. Stroke trainers are also being integrated. I\'m building out a detailed Kanji section with robust search features and visual stroke guides.\n\nI\'m also working on minigames and educational games, with a memory game using Kanji/Kana \342\206\224 translation cards. I am designing a real-time JLPT quiz covering grammar, particles, and vocabulary, along with an instant PT-BR explanation and XP score. I\'ve also planned a sentence-building challenge.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Exercises**\n\nI\'m now detailing interactive exercises, including word matching and a time-based character/word connection game. I\'m also planning flashcards with spaced repetition, auto-assessment, and retention stats. A key focus is an AI assistant, powered by Gemini, that explains grammar, analyzes sentences, and creates personalized quizzes.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 161936170
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
