  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Core Types**\n\nI\'ve started building the foundational types for the project. Specifically, `JLPTLevel` is now a union of strings representing the levels. I\'m also thinking about structuring `KanaItem` with its properties. Next up is constructing the dataset structure to support the educational materials.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the structures for `KanjiItem`, `VocabItem`, `GrammarItem`, and the challenge types. Thinking about incorporating all of these key elements (mnemonic, examples, and audio) into each data type is the current focus. I\'m also planning the UserStats and Achievement system.\n\n\n\n**Structuring Grammar Components**\n\nI\'m deep in the weeds of `grammarData.ts`, aiming for comprehensive JLPT grammar points, including conjugations and PT-BR explanations. I\'m building out sentence puzzles in `sentenceData.ts` and crafting a rich offline question set with AI generation capabilities in `quizData.ts`. The organization by JLPT level and category (Verbs, Adjectives, Nouns, etc.) is key to this phase.\n\n\n**Designing User Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into interface components. The goal is a user-friendly and feature-rich learning experience. I\'ve built the `AudioButton` for seamless pronunciation, alongside `Header.tsx` for easy navigation, including XP, streak, level, sound control, and Sensei status. Also, the `KanaExplorer` with its interactive charts, stroke practice, and audio support is completed. I\'m also planning the design for the `KanjiDictionary` with its interactive filters and drawing canvas, as well as the comprehensive `VocabGrammarHub` with JLPT filters. Lastly, the `GamesHub` is taking shape with the Memory Match game.\n\n\n**Developing Game Modules**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing game modules to enhance the learning experience! I\'m creating \"Vocab \342\206\224 Tradu\303\247\303\243o,\" a matching game with combos, a timer, score, animations, and even a victory sound. I\'m building \"Montador de Frases\" with drag-and-click functionality and \"Quiz JLPT Showdown\" with timed multiple-choice questions and streak multipliers. \"Kana Rush\" provides a fast-paced character recognition test.\nI\'ve also introduced \"Sensei Kenji,\" an AI tutor, powered by Gemini 3.7 Flash, in `SenseiChat.tsx`. A sentence analyzer for furigana and grammatical breakdowns is also in progress. I\'m incorporating an interactive kanji drawing canvas and a user progress modal for badges, XP, and level tracking.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 4767667
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
