    thinking: "**Analyzing the Data Request**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user\'s request. It seems they want me to gather all the kanji from JLPT N5, N4, and N3 levels, specifically and including the minigames. So far, I am focused on the first point: *N5, N4 e N3 Kanjis Data*. I am starting with the N5 level.\n\n\n**Gathering More Kanji**\n\nI\'ve moved on to gathering the kanji for N5. Now, I\'m working through the kanji for JLPT N4. I\'ve compiled a list that encompasses various categories like people, body, actions, and modifiers. I\'m taking care to organize everything systematically. The goal is a comprehensive list ready for the user, with no repetition of N5 kanji.\n\n\n**Expanding the Kanji List**\n\nI\'m now integrating N3 kanji into the list, ensuring I cover the official syllabus, including everything from actions and emotions to political and economic terms. This builds on the foundation of N5 and N4. I\'m also ensuring no kanji is repeated. Moreover, I\'m thinking about the \"Jogo da Mem\303\263ria\" game and how I can utilize this new data.\n\n\n"
