  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Interconnections**\n\nI\'m now diving into the interactions between files handling grammar and vocabulary data. I\'ve begun to examine `sentenceData.ts` and `quizData.ts` for potential synergies. Additionally, I\'m exploring the best way to modularize `grammarData.ts` and `vocabData.ts`, aiming to split them by JLPT level for better organization.\n\n\n**Structuring Grammar Points**\n\nI\'ve outlined a modular structure for grammar data, planning to divide files by JLPT level (N5, N4, etc.). Each file, such as `/src/data/grammarN5.ts`, will contain comprehensive grammar points. This approach aims to keep the data clean, manageable, and avoid token limit issues or file clutter. The detailed contents for each file have also been enumerated.\n\n\n**Defining Grammar Structures**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on expanding the grammar structures for `/src/data/grammarN3.ts`. I\'m meticulously adding N3 grammar points like \343\200\234\343\202\217\343\201\221\343\201\247\343\201\257\343\201\252\343\201\204 and \343\200\234\343\201\206\343\201\241\343\201\253, ensuring each entry aligns with the planned structure. It\'s a challenging but rewarding task to categorize these various structures effectively. I am also working on categorizing grammar points and related expressions in multiple ways, to maximize usability.\n\n\n**Expanding Grammar Points**\n\nI\'m now adding N2 and N1 grammar to `/src/data/grammarN2N1.ts`. I\'m populating this file with a variety of structures, including \343\201\253\351\201\225\343\201\204\343\201\252\343\201\204, \343\201\253\345\237\272\343\201\245\343\201\204\343\201\246, and \343\201\253\343\201\227\343\201\237\343\201\214\343\201\243\343\201\246. I am also working on categorizing vocabulary, specifically structuring `/src/data/vocabN5.ts` and `/src/data/vocabN4.ts`. This effort involves comprehensive categorization, including verbs, adjectives, nouns, adverbs, and example sentences.\n\n\n**Categorizing Vocabulary Further**\n\nI\'m now expanding the vocabulary data organization. I\'m adding comprehensive lists for N4, N3, and combined N2/N1 levels, focusing on specific themes and categories within each. I\'m also confirming the inclusion of \'substantivo\' in `VocabCategory` and ensuring it\'s present in the category filter chips within `VocabGrammarHub.tsx` to ensure comprehensive coverage.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 16
      nanos: 884265008
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
