    thinking: "**Enriching Kanji Data**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the user\'s request, specifically the addition of more N2 and N1 kanji. I plan to enhance `/src/data/kanjiN2N1.ts` with dozens of essential kanji. These additions will include radicals, stroke counts, on\'yomi and kun\'yomi readings, and detailed Portuguese translations. This will greatly improve the dataset.\n\n\n**Adding Example Sentences**\n\nI\'ve made progress adding example sentences with furigana and translations for essential N2 and N1 kanji. I am including the specific kanji requested by the user, such as \346\206\262, \350\262\277, \344\274\201, and others, adding both English and Portuguese translations. I believe this will significantly enhance understanding.\n\n\n**Expanding Kanji List**\n\nI\'ve integrated a new batch of Kanji into the dataset. This includes kanji such as \350\224\275, \350\262\252, \345\202\262, and others, along with translations. The work now shifts toward implementing these kanji within the minigame functionality to boost the user\'s experience.\n\n\n\n**Developing Grammar Database**\n\nI am now focusing on expanding the grammar database. I\'m actively working on adding comprehensive N2 and N1 grammar points to `/src/data/grammarN2N1.ts`. This includes patterns, Portuguese titles, categories, formation formulas, detailed explanations, and key rules for JLPT preparation. I am incorporating multiple real-world examples with Japanese, furigana, romaji, and Portuguese translations, starting with grammar points like `\343\200\234\343\201\253\351\201\225\343\201\204\343\201\252\343\201\204`, `\343\200\234\343\201\253\345\237\272\343\201\245\343\201\204\343\201\246`, and others.\n\n\n**Adding Grammar to Dataset**\n\nI\'ve just added several more N1 grammar points to the database. I\'ve focused on complex structures like `\343\200\234\343\201\253\351\201\225\343\201\204\343\201\252\343\201\204`, `\343\200\234\343\201\253\345\237\272\343\201\245\343\201\204\343\201\246`, and now also added `\343\200\234\343\201\253\351\231\220\343\202\213`, `\343\200\234\343\201\215\343\202\214\343\201\252\343\201\204`, `\343\200\234\343\201\214\343\201\241`, and others. This set includes patterns, Portuguese titles, categories, formation formulas, and detailed examples, complete with Japanese, furigana, romaji, and Portuguese translations. I\'m aiming for full JLPT N1 coverage.\n\n\n**Incorporating Grammar Patterns**\n\nI\'ve just added several more grammar points to the dataset, focusing on N1 patterns. I\'ve integrated `~\343\201\276\343\201\230\343\201\215`, `~\346\245\265\343\201\276\343\202\212\343\201\252\343\201\204`, `~\343\202\222\347\232\256\345\210\207\343\202\212\343\201\253`, `~\343\201\247\343\201\202\343\202\214`, and `~\344\275\231\345\204\200\343\201\252\343\201\217\343\201\225\343\202\214\343\202\213`. These include Portuguese translations and detailed examples. I am also planning to review `vocabN2N1.ts` for completeness and compatibility.\n\n\n"
